WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.276 --> 00:00:04.580
(pensive music)
(text buzzing)

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.280
- [Narrator] May 1st, 2003.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.590
The US declares war
victory in Afghanistan.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.930
- The bulk of this country today

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.120
is permissive, it's secure.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.920
- [Narrator] The Taliban
had been toppled only months

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.410
after 9/11, and there were
some 13,000 NATO troops

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:19.870
in the country.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.800
Fast forward nearly 20 years.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.940
American soldiers have left,
the Taliban have come back,

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.050
and the United Nations
says civilian deaths

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.080
of women and children in Afghanistan

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.740
have hit record levels.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.540
While it's difficult to map exactly

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.200
how much territory the
group actually controls,

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.250
limited data suggests it's
more than half of the country

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.980
with the insurgents claiming authority

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.370
over major border crossings
and infrastructure.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.990
- Many people, both inside
and outside the country

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:46.896
have been surprised by the speed

00:00:46.896 --> 00:00:49.730
and the scale of the Taliban's advances,

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:50.770
and by how fragile

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.860
the Afghan government's
authority is looking.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.610
- It's time to end America's longest war.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.130
It's time for American
troops to come home.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.610
- [Narrator] Before Biden ordered
America's troops to leave,

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:03.040
the US had been trying
to exit for a while.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.750
- And by the end of next year,

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.997
our war in Afghanistan will be over.

00:01:07.997 --> 00:01:09.590
- [Narrator] But Taliban victories meant

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:10.950
that US soldiers remained

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.970
in the country much longer than intended.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.680
- [Sune] And now the
foreign troops have gone

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.220
and the Taliban is steadily
taking over larger parts

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.120
of the country.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.410
- [Narrator] Here's
how the insurgent group

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.700
has expanded to become stronger
than it's been in 20 years,

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.700
creating the conditions
for potential chaos

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.500
as US troops leave behind a country

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.023
on the brink of civil war.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:30.730
At the beginning of the war,

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.610
America's campaign in Afghanistan
reached some milestones

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:34.890
in just a few months.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.440
- When the US-led coalition
invaded Afghanistan,

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.870
the Taliban had controlled
the country for five years

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.150
after taking power following

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.313
an extremely violent civil war.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.970
They'd imposed strick
Islamic rule on Afghanistan.

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:48.920
All that changed after 9/11

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.300
when President Bush set out

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.020
to punish the group for
harboring Al-Qaeda terrorists.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.220
- The United States
military has begun strikes

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.870
against Al-Qaeda terrorist training camps

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.340
and military installations

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.860
of the Taliban regime in Afghanistan.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.650
- [Narrator] Bush deployed
some 2,500 US troops

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.700
into the country,

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.780
causing the Taliban to abandon Kabul,

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.930
and soon thereafter Kandahar,
their main stronghold.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.670
- The Taliban were a
broken force at that time.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.050
They gave up barely without a fight

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:18.830
and melted back into society,

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.900
and retreated into villages.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.010
Some Taliban commanders actually offered

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.270
to surrender in return for amnesty

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.170
but the US declined that offer

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:29.470
and wanted to keep fighting them.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.580
They wanted to stamp out

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.920
every last terrorist from Afghanistan.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.180
Instead, the Taliban regrouped in Pakistan

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.410
where they received shelter and support

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.010
with the aim of returning later.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.660
- [Narrator] The Taliban
began their resurgence

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.030
and by the middle of the decade,

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.120
they had launched hundreds

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.580
of suicide attacks and
thousands of bombings,

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.615
killing hundreds of US soldiers.

00:02:49.615 --> 00:02:51.620
(helicopter whirring)

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.550
So to counter their renewed presence,

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:56.842
Obama began deploying
more forces in the region.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.846
- The United States has
conducted an operation

00:02:58.846 --> 00:03:00.897
that killed Osama bin Laden,

00:03:00.897 --> 00:03:02.280
the leader of Al-Qaeda.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.730
- [Narrator] May 1st, 2011,

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:06.030
Osama bin Laden, the man held responsible

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.500
for the 9/11 attacks was killed

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.570
and around that period,

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:12.360
the number of US troops
in Afghanistan hit a peak

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.393
of around 100,000.

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:16.850
(gun firing)

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.670
But policymakers and experts began

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:19.990
to question the effectiveness

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.770
of that large military presence.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:22.670
- What became clear

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.050
was that the US counterinsurgency strategy

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.240
did not eradicate the Taliban.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.380
In fact, some of the more
controversial tactics

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:30.950
that the US used in Afghanistan,

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:33.740
such as night raids and
arbitrary detentions,

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:36.300
and air strikes that
sometimes killed civilians

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.720
created this contempt
in local communities,

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.200
and actually helped the
Taliban recruit more fighters.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.040
- [Narrator] The Taliban's
recruitment drive enabled them

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.420
to increase in numbers

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.740
and gain control of yet more territory,

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.120
launching near daily attacks

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.630
against the US and Afghan forces.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.980
So with bin Laden dead and
facing mounting pressure

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:56.330
from Democratic lawmakers in Congress,

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.610
Obama announced his plan to
withdraw some 33,000 troops

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:01.210
from the region and transfer power

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:02.750
to the Afghan military.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:06.540
- Our mission will change
from combat to support.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.030
By 2014, this process of
transition will be complete,

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.540
and the Afghan people will be responsible

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:14.760
for their own security.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.620
- That plan didn't work as intended.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.440
The Afghan security forces were plagued

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.640
by problems that continued to haunt them,

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.320
such as corruption, which made them

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.040
an ineffective fighting
force against the Taliban

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.220
who continued to fight,

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.240
allegedly armed and funded by Pakistan.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.180
- [Narrator] The Afghan government
has acknowledged problems

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.230
with effectiveness and corruption
among its security forces

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:37.150
but told The Journal that
corruption is decreasing.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:40.200
And Pakistan's government has
denied backing the Taliban

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.540
but says it has some limited
influence over the group.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.560
This map shows just how much territory

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.750
the Taliban had taken over in 2017.

00:04:48.622 --> 00:04:49.830
- [Sune] The Taliban's gradual advances

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:52.180
across the country really
began alarming people

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.100
in the capital.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.410
- [Narrator] After NATO announced the end

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.708
of its combat mission,

00:04:55.708 --> 00:04:56.630
(lively music)

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:58.480
the Taliban scored symbolic victory,

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.568
such as capturing the city of Kunduz.

00:05:00.568 --> 00:05:02.530
(guns firing)

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.470
While mapping the
Taliban's exactly presence

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.780
has been tricky in such a fluid situation,

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.810
some analysts have drawn maps based

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:10.770
on news reports and social media

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:14.370
that outline the group's
territorial control from 2017.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.970
At the time, the Afghan military

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:18.650
was already struggling
to hold the Taliban back,

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.040
and Trump announced he
was sending more troops.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:24.215
- The security threats
we face in Afghanistan,

00:05:24.215 --> 00:05:26.980
and the broader region are immense.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:29.040
- President Trump's
announcement fueled the will

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.570
to fight among some fighters.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:33.220
I remember speaking to
young Taliban fighters

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.830
who said that they'd actually
considered giving up the war

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.530
once the American troops left.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:40.450
But once President Trump said
he was gonna send more troops,

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:41.340
they said there was no way

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.930
they were gonna give up the fight.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.850
- [Narrator] Around four years
later, on July 4th, 2021,

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:47.990
US troops finally left Bagram,

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.500
their main base of
operations in the country.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:53.400
Meanwhile, the Taliban's
expansion accelerated.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:57.090
- We cannot continue
this cycle of extending

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.860
or expanding our military
presence in Afghanistan.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.140
- [Narrator] As foreign troops pulled out,

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.550
insurgents took many districts

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.120
without having to fight.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.620
The group has been trying
to show a friendlier face,

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.490
posting propaganda videos purporting

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.370
to show Taliban fighters shaking hands

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.920
with Afghan soldiers

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:14.636
or guarding borders
without disrupting trade.

00:06:14.636 --> 00:06:19.210
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:20.660
- [Narrator] The Afghan
government didn't respond

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:23.130
to a request for comment on these images.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.720
Analysts say it's part of a campaign

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.580
to legitimize the insurgency

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.053
amid negotiations with
the Afghan government.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.850
While the Biden administration

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:33.570
says America's military campaign

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.480
has accomplished its objectives,

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.300
US air strikes against the Taliban

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.060
are expected to continue.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:42.540
And America plans to keep
monitoring terrorist threats.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.040
People in Afghanistan question

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.810
what the Taliban's plans are,

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:48.420
and whether they can coexist
with the Afghan government.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:52.270
- The Taliban's gains raise
two main risks for Afghanistan.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.370
One, that the country might split possibly

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:55.750
along sectarian lines,

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.350
which could throw the country
into another bloody civil war,

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.050
or that a fundamentalist
Islamist group takes power

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.170
in Afghanistan again,

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.710
which would undermine the
whole purpose of the war,

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:07.759
which was to eradicate terrorism
risks from the country.

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:10.509
(dramatic music)

